# Third-party notices

`crates/core/src/native_palette.rs` ports Material Color Utilities 0.13.0
quantization (Google LLC, Apache-2.0) and Dart SDK Random compatibility
(The Dart Authors, BSD-3-Clause). Full notices and licenses are packaged in
`assets/licenses/native_palette.txt`. The native SQLite/TTML data jobs use
rusqlite 0.40.2 and roxmltree 0.21.1 under their MIT licenses, packaged in
`assets/licenses/native_data_jobs.txt`.

The English title-casing control flow in
`crates/core/src/metadata/musicbrainz/casing.rs` follows
`golang.org/x/text/cases`. Its frozen Unicode 15 data is generated using the
public Go APIs. No Go runtime is linked into
the Rust backend. Retain this notice in source and binary distributions.
The artwork resampling in `crates/core/src/cover.rs` also follows the
ApproxBiLinear pixel-center and premultiplied-alpha calculations from
`golang.org/x/image/draw`, under the same Go Authors BSD license below.
URL reference parsing and serialization in `crates/network/src/url.rs` follow
`net/url`, also under that license.

